<MainLayout title={title} description={description}><section class="hero"><div class="wrap"><p class="eyebrow">Mason City, Iowa</p><h1>Drain Cleaning That Gets to the Clog</h1><p>Clogged drain, backed-up basement floor drain, slow kitchen sink, or a main sewer line that keeps plugging up? A-1 Drain Cleaning clears residential and commercial drains and sewer lines in Mason City and surrounding North Iowa communities.</p><p><a class="btn" href="tel:6415302728">Call 641-530-2728</a></p></div></section><section class="section"><div class="wrap"><p class="eyebrow">Drain & sewer work</p><h2>Common Problems We Clear</h2><div class="grid cards"><article class="card"><h3>Main Sewer Line Clogs</h3><p>Whole-house backup, multiple slow drains, sewage at the basement floor drain, or a sewer that keeps backing up.</p><a href="/services/main-sewer-line-cleaning/">Main sewer line cleaning</a></article><article class="card"><h3>Tree Roots in Sewer Lines</h3><p>Recurring backups and roots growing through older sewer pipe joints can keep a line plugged after ordinary snaking.</p><a href="/services/tree-roots/">Tree root removal</a></article><article class="card"><h3>Basement Floor Drains</h3><p>A basement drain backing up when the washer runs or several fixtures are used can point to a blockage farther down the line.</p><a href="/services/basement-floor-drain/">Basement drain cleaning</a></article><article class="card"><h3>Kitchen, Bath & Toilet Clogs</h3><p>Slow sinks, tubs, showers and clogged toilets are handled with equipment matched to the line and blockage.</p><a href="/services/drain-cleaning/">Drain cleaning</a></article></div></div></section><section class="section dark"><div class="wrap"><p class="eyebrow">Local sewer problems</p><h2>Older Homes, Root Intrusion & Repeat Clogs</h2><p>Mason City has a lot of older housing. When a sewer line repeatedly plugs, the question is not only how to open the pipe today. It is what keeps causing the blockage. Roots, buildup, damaged joints and other pipe problems can turn a one-time clog into a recurring one.</p><p>When needed, cleaning can be paired with sewer camera inspection to see what is actually inside the line.</p></div></section><section class="section" id="faq"><div class="wrap faq"><p class="eyebrow">Questions</p><h2>Drain Cleaning FAQ</h2><details><summary>Why is my basement floor drain backing up?</summary><p>The floor drain is one of the lowest drains in a house. If wastewater backs up there while other fixtures are running, the blockage may be farther down the main sewer line.</p></details><details><summary>Why do tree roots keep clogging my sewer line?</summary><p>Roots can enter through cracks, joints and damaged sections of buried sewer pipe. Cutting the roots can restore flow, but recurring problems may require finding the damaged section.</p></details><details><summary>What does it mean when several drains back up at once?</summary><p>When a toilet, shower and floor drain are affected together, the problem is more likely in the main drain or sewer line than in one fixture.</p></details><details><summary>Do you clean main sewer lines in Mason City?</summary><p>Yes. A-1 Drain Cleaning handles main sewer line blockages and drain problems in Mason City and surrounding North Iowa communities.</p></details></div></section></MainLayout>